course: dictionary
lesson: 3200
title: Enforce: making people follow the rules
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To enforce means to make sure people obey a law or rule. Police enforce the law on the roads, and a referee enforces the rules of a match. Enforce is a verb, so it changes: enforces, enforced, enforcing.
explain: The second meaning is stronger: to make something happen by force or strong pressure. «Enforced silence» is silence that people were made to keep, not silence they chose.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «It was reported that some countries planned or made rules keeping children under 16 off social media» tells you there are rules. «Others say it is hard to enforce» tells you the difficult part is making people obey those rules.
fact: Enforce is a verb: enforce, enforces, enforced, enforcing.
fact: «Enforce» means to make sure people obey a law or rule.
fact: «Enforced» can also mean made to happen by force or strong pressure, as in «enforced silence».
fact: «Law enforcement» is the work of police and others who make sure the laws are obeyed.
fact: To check your meaning, swap in «make sure people follow» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Police officers enforce the law on the roads.» What does enforce mean here? | To write brand-new laws for the country | To break the law on purpose | To ignore the noise of the traffic | *To make sure people obey the law
exercise: The head teacher says the phone rule will be strictly enforced. What does strictly enforced suggest? | The rule has been forgotten by everyone | *The rule is always made sure to be obeyed, with no exceptions | The rule is always made sure to be obeyed | The rule was made up as a joke
exercise: «The library was filled with enforced silence.» What does enforced silence mean? | A quiet nap on a sunny afternoon | A loud party with music | Silence that people chose to keep for fun | *Silence that people were made to keep
test: «Some say the new rule is hard to enforce.» What does enforce mean in this sentence? | To cheer for the rule | To make the rule longer | To forget the rule | *To make sure people obey the rule
test: Which phrase means the work of making sure the laws are obeyed? | Law breaking | Law writing | *Law enforcement | Lawn mowing
exam: «Some countries planned rules to keep children off social media, but it is hard to enforce them.» What does enforce mean in this sentence? | To make the rules longer | To cheer for the rules | To forget the rules | *To make sure people obey the rules
